**Author**: Rich Nunley
**Related Spec**: specs/441-continue-an-explicit-execute-queue-after-the-previous-issue-is-delivered/

# File: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-execute.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/523-clean-up-the-issue-branch-and-sync-the-default-branch-after-successful-delivery/requirements.md
Feature: Clean up the issue branch and sync the default branch after successful delivery

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Delivered branch is cleaned up and the default branch is synced
    Given issue #42 is proven delivered on clean local branch "42-example" at head H
    And remote branch "42-example" points at H
    When the controller records the terminal delivery for #42
    Then remote and local branch "42-example" are deleted
    And the checkout is the default branch fast-forwarded to origin
    And the output contains "#42: MERGED and CLOSED" followed by "#42: branch cleanup: deleted 42-example and fast-forwarded main"
    And the controller exits 0

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Remote branch already absent
    Given issue #42 is proven delivered on clean local branch "42-example" at head H
    And remote branch "42-example" does not exist
    When the controller records the terminal delivery for #42
    Then no remote warning is printed
    And the checkout, fast-forward pull, and local branch deletion complete as in SCN001

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Unsafe cleanup is skipped with a warning
    Given issue #42 is proven delivered
    And the worktree is dirty outside ".nmg-sdlc/", the local head differs, the checkout fails, or the pull is not a fast-forward
    When the controller records the terminal delivery for #42
    Then the output contains "#42: MERGED and CLOSED" and "#42: branch cleanup skipped: <reasonCode>" naming that condition
    And no later cleanup step runs and the local branch and uncommitted changes are preserved
    And the controller exits 0

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Remote branch moved after merge
    Given issue #42 is proven delivered at head H
    And remote branch "42-example" points at a commit other than H
    When the controller records the terminal delivery for #42
    Then remote branch "42-example" still exists
    And the output contains "#42: remote branch cleanup skipped: remote_head_mismatch"
    And local cleanup completes as in SCN001

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Cleanup runs per issue in a queue and on re-entry
    Given "/sdlc-execute #42 #43" delivers #42, or bare "/sdlc-execute" starts on already-delivered branch "42-example"
    When the controller records #42's terminal delivery
    Then #42's cleanup runs before the next queued issue starts
    And the next issue starts from the synced default branch
